    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` feature end-to-end, following the existing Spring MVC / OpenAPI-codegen / MapStruct conventions in the codebase.\n\n**Behavior:** A `POST /api/owners` request may now include an ISO `birthDate`. When present, the owner's `ageBand` is derived and returned on reads \u2014 `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+) \u2014 computed as full years between `birthDate` and the owner's `registrationDate`. When no birth date is supplied, `ageBand` is absent.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added an optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema (request input) and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema (response). These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` DTOs.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 mapped `ageBand` via a new `formatAgeBand(owner)` helper that uses `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)`, falling back to the current date only if `registrationDate` is null, and returns `null` (field omitted) when there's no birth date. `birthDate` maps by name automatically in both directions.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, along with the entire existing suite.",
